v = p.v - n.v. SoC itself is not clamped; only the lookup is limited to [0, 1].
`stored_voltage` reports OCV and `stored_current` reports discharge current.

Defaults represent the Leaf ZE1 40 kWh pack. The NMC 811 / graphite-SiOx LG M50
OCV table [CHEN-2020], derived from PyBaMM Chen2020 at 10 % SoC steps, is the
course's stand-in (assumed): the ZE1's own chemistry differs. Voltages are scaled
by Ns. R0 and capacity retain Battery's Nissan/INL defaults for comparison.
R1/R0 and tau1 use pulse 5 (approximately 60 % SoC, 25 C) of the ORNL Leaf
33.1 Ah cell 1-RC fit [ORNL-LEAF-ECM] (derived).

The equation tau1 * der(v1) = R1 * i - v1 is equivalent to C1 = tau1/R1.
Using tau1 avoids division by R1 and permits R1 = 0 with v1 initially zero.

